{"id":"A2-L026","title":"Past Continuous: production and review","cefr":"A2","level":"A2","unit":"A2-U02","focus":"Past Continuous — produção e revisão","targets":{"grammar":"Past Continuous — produção e revisão","pron":"Ligação entre palavras","verbs":[],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["scene","background","suddenly","interrupt","narrate","character","setting","climax","narrator","storyline","dialogue","flashback","suspense","twist","resolution","theme"],"field":"Compras","genre":"Transcrição de palestra e podcast","skill":"Escrita","words_min":16},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 26 · Past Continuous: production and review","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Past Continuous — produção e revisão.","**Pronúncia:** Ligação entre palavras.","**10 palavras novas** (compras).","**Texto do dia:** transcrição de palestra e podcast."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (A2):** eu consigo ouvir uma palestra e escrever frases com o contínuo no passado."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["Você começa a praticar tarefas curtas no formato das provas.","Esta aula treina **escrever frases claras e corretas (IELTS Writing, TOEFL Writing)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["scene","cena"],["background","plano de fundo"],["suddenly","de repente"],["interrupt","interromper"],["narrate","narrar"],["character","personagem"],["setting","cenário"],["climax","clímax"],["narrator","narrator"],["storyline","storyline"],["dialogue","dialogue"],["flashback","flashback"],["suspense","suspense"],["twist","twist"],["resolution","resolution"],["theme","theme"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A lecture transcript","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Lecture: Interrupted Actions","paras":["Today we study how to tell stories. First, set the scene with the **Past Continuous**: “It **was raining** and I **was walking**.” Then add an event with the **Past Simple**: “Suddenly, a car **stopped**.”","Notice: the long action is background; the short action is the main event. Use **while** for two long actions: “While I **was reading**, she **was cooking**.”"],"kicker":"LECTURE TRANSCRIPT","by":"Prof. Ames","gloss":[["scene","cena"],["background","plano de fundo"],["suddenly","de repente"],["interrupt","interromper"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"The long action is the background.","ans":"T","why":"long action = background."},{"q":"We use while for one short action.","ans":"F","why":"two long actions."},{"q":"The professor teaches storytelling.","ans":"T","why":"tell stories."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“suddenly” means…","opts":["de repente","devagar","sempre"],"ans":0,"why":"suddenly."},{"q":"“interrupt” means…","opts":["interromper","repetir","esquecer"],"ans":0,"why":"interrupt."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Storytelling with tenses","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Papel","Tempo","Exemplo"],"rows":[["cena","Past Continuous","**It was raining.**"],["evento","Past Simple","**A car stopped.**"],["duas ações longas","while + contínuo","**While I was reading, she was cooking.**"]],"cap":"Storytelling with tenses"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Organize: cena → evento → resultado."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"It ___ when a car stopped. (rain)","a":"was raining","why":"cena."},{"s":"While I ___ , she cooked. (read)","a":"was reading","why":"while."},{"s":"Suddenly, a car ___ . (stop)","a":"stopped","why":"evento."},{"s":"We ___ the lights. (notice)","a":"noticed","why":"simples."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["scene","cena"],["background","plano de fundo"],["suddenly","de repente"],["interrupt","interromper"],["narrate","narrar"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["scene","Set","the"],"ans":"Set the scene","pt":"Monte a cena."},{"words":["the","event","Now","add"],"ans":"Now add the event","pt":"Agora acrescente o evento."}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"scene","pos":"word","pt":"cena","ex":"Set the scene.","expt":"Monte a cena."},{"w":"background","pos":"word","pt":"plano de fundo","ex":"In the background.","expt":"Ao fundo."},{"w":"suddenly","pos":"word","pt":"de repente","ex":"Suddenly, it rained.","expt":"De repente, choveu."},{"w":"interrupt","pos":"word","pt":"interromper","ex":"Don’t interrupt.","expt":"Não interrompa."},{"w":"narrate","pos":"word","pt":"narrar","ex":"Narrate the story.","expt":"Narre a história."},{"w":"character","pos":"word","pt":"personagem","ex":"A funny character.","expt":"Um personagem engraçado."},{"w":"setting","pos":"word","pt":"cenário","ex":"A quiet setting.","expt":"Um cenário calmo."},{"w":"climax","pos":"word","pt":"clímax","ex":"The story’s climax.","expt":"O clímax da história."},{"w":"narrator","pos":"word","pt":"narrator","ex":"narrador","expt":"The narrator speaks."},{"w":"storyline","pos":"word","pt":"storyline","ex":"trama","expt":"A simple storyline."},{"w":"dialogue","pos":"word","pt":"dialogue","ex":"diálogo","expt":"A short dialogue."},{"w":"flashback","pos":"word","pt":"flashback","ex":"flashback","expt":"A quick flashback."},{"w":"suspense","pos":"word","pt":"suspense","ex":"suspense","expt":"High suspense."},{"w":"twist","pos":"word","pt":"twist","ex":"reviravolta","expt":"A surprise twist."},{"w":"resolution","pos":"word","pt":"resolution","ex":"desfecho","expt":"A happy resolution."},{"w":"theme","pos":"word","pt":"theme","ex":"tema","expt":"The main theme."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**Set the scene.** — Monte a cena.","**It was raining and I was walking.** — Estava chovendo e eu caminhava.","**Now add the event.** — Agora acrescente o evento.","**Better than nothing.** — Melhor que nada.","**Better luck next time.** — Mais sorte da próxima vez.","**Out of sight, out of mind.** — Longe dos olhos, longe do coração.","**Actions speak louder than words.** — Ações valem mais que palavras."]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"paint","pt":"pintar","forms":[["I / you / we / they paint","I paint walls."],["he / she / it paints","He paints boats."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Story class","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Story class","lines":[["Teacher","Set the scene.","Monte a cena."],["Ana","It was raining and I was walking.","Estava chovendo e eu caminhava."],["Teacher","Now add the event.","Agora acrescente o evento."],["Ana","Suddenly, a car stopped.","De repente, um carro parou."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Ligação entre palavras","items":[{"label":"Ligação entre palavras","note":"Consoante final liga à vogal seguinte: pick it up → pi-ki-tup.","words":["pick it up","turn it off","an apple","check in"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Tell a mini-story with scene + event.","pt":"Conte.","model":"It was raining. Suddenly, a car stopped."},{"q":"Use while with two actions.","pt":"Use.","model":"While I was reading, she was cooking."},{"q":"Say what interrupted you.","pt":"Diga.","model":"The phone rang."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a 6-line mini-story using both tenses.","model":"It was raining and I was walking home. I was listening to music. Suddenly, a car stopped. A man opened the door. He gave me an umbrella. I smiled.","checklist":["Usei **cena + evento**","Usei **while/when/suddenly**","6 linhas"],"words":"6 linhas"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note"